const alternateSamples={"sbar":{"good":["In this fictional training session, participants received two different room locations.","The booking changed after the first invitation was sent.","The conflicting messages could leave participants waiting in the wrong place.","Please confirm the correct room with the organizer and issue one clear update.","Confirm who sends the update and how participants who miss it will be directed."],"poor":["There is confusion.","The room was discussed.","People will work it out.","Please deal with it.","I sent a message, so it is finished."]},"teach":{"good":["For this fictional orientation activity, sign in at the confirmed training room before joining the group.","To check that I explained the arrangement clearly, where will you go first?","I will join the group first and sign in if there is time.","Thank you. I need to clarify the order. Sign in first, then join the group. How would you describe those steps now?"],"poor":["Just follow the orientation instructions.","Everything clear?","Probably.","Then we can move on."]},"qi":{"good":["Participants in a fictional learning session sometimes receive an outdated room location.","With the organizer’s approval, test a single final-location confirmation for one session.","Count conflicting location messages using a consistent definition before and during the test.","Check whether the confirmation creates extra messages or delays the invitation.","The organizer and participants will review the results and decide whether to keep or adapt the change."],"poor":["Nobody reads invitations.","Send many more reminders to everyone.","Count how many messages were sent.","More messages cannot cause any problems.","Assume attendance proves the change worked."]},"cus":{"good":["I am concerned that two fictional training participants are about to use materials labeled with different versions.","I am uncomfortable continuing until we verify which version is approved for this session.","This could create a safety-learning problem if inconsistent instructions are taught.","Please check the approved version with the responsible organizer before we proceed; escalate unresolved concerns through the relevant route."],"poor":["These materials look strange.","This is annoying.","You brought the wrong files again.","I have mentioned it, so it is your problem."]},"desc":{"good":["During the fictional learning session, questions were answered before the participant finished speaking.","I am concerned that we may miss what the participant is actually asking.","Could we pause until the person finishes, then check our understanding?","This could make the discussion clearer and reduce repeated explanations. Can we try it together?"],"poor":["You do not know how to listen.","Everyone agrees that you are rude.","Let someone else do the talking.","If you continue, I will embarrass you in front of the group."]},"huddle":{"good":["Prepare a fictional orientation session using one confirmed room location and one materials version.","Ari confirms the booking; Jamie checks the materials version; Robin sends the location update.","The booking confirmation has changed and one shared folder still contains an older handout.","Regroup before distribution. Use only the version confirmed by the organizer and direct arrivals to the confirmed room.","Compare the actual arrival experience with the plan, then agree one improvement for the next session."],"poor":["Run a good session.","Whoever has time can sort it out.","Changes happen; no need to discuss them.","People will ask if they are confused.","No complaints means no improvements are needed."]},"fishbone":{"good":["Participants in a fictional orientation receive conflicting location information.","Different organizers assume someone else sends the final confirmation.","The booking change process does not include a final invitation check.","A shared invitation template retains the prior location.","The booking changes shortly before the session, while organizers are handling other tasks.","Review the message sequence, booking-change process, and template history; ask organizers how responsibility was understood. These are possible contributors, not established causes."],"poor":["Attendance is poor.","Participants are careless.","The whole booking system is useless.","The software must be broken.","The workplace is always chaotic.","The cause is obvious from one complaint."]}};
